            <ArticleTitle>Two new Anti-TMV active chalconoid analogues from the root of Phyllanthus emblica.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2143-2148</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/14786419.2017.1280487</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two new chalconoid analogues, emblirol A (1) and B (2), along with three known ones (3-5), were isolated from the root of the Phyllanthus emblica L. Their structures were elucidated on the basis of spectral data. Compound 1 and 2 showed moderate anti-TMV activity with inhibition rates 79.6 and 62.1% at a concentration of 1 mg/mL, respectively.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
